==List of Munakata high priests==
'''Munakata Daiguushi''' (宗像大宮司) refers to the chief priest of {{ill|Munakata Taisha|ja|宗像大社|qq=draft}} located in present‐day {{ill|Fukuoka Prefecture|ja|福岡県|qq=draft}} {{ill|Munakata City|ja|宗像市|qq=draft}}. The office of Daiguushi was exclusively held by the {{ill|Munakata clan|ja|宗像氏|1=Munakata clan|fr|Clan Munakata|qq=draft}} until the main line of the Munakata Daiguushi family became extinct; nowadays the shrines have been divided into three.
